{"id": "EUVD-2026-71301", "enisaUuid": "c707bfeb-0d7f-383c-acc9-59330879ef24", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ngtp: serialize PDP context updates\n\nPDP contexts can be deleted through GTP_CMD_DELPDP or while the GTP\nnetwork device is being unregistered. The latter is serialized by RTNL,\nbut the generic-netlink delete path only holds RCU.\n\nRunning both paths concurrently can therefore make both paths delete the\nsame PDP context. The issue was found through static analysis and\nreproduced on a KASAN-enabled kernel by a simple two-thread program\nracing GTP_CMD_DELPDP against RTM_DELLINK:\n\n  Oops: general protection fault, probably for non-canonical address\n  KASAN: maybe wild-memory-access in range\n         [0xdead000000000120-0xdead000000000127]\n  RIP: gtp_genl_del_pdp+0x1c1/0x420 [gtp]\n  RBP: dead000000000122\n\nThe second deletion dereferenced the poisoned hlist pprev pointer.\n\nSerialize gtp_pdp_add(), gtp_genl_del_pdp(), and gtp_dellink() with a\nshared mutex. Keep the mutex held until the final use of a PDP context in\nthe NEWPDP path, and keep the RCU read-side section around the complete\nPDP context use in the DELPDP path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:55:01", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b4ac2a5ce5a96ec21ed48f60d30b52b1fb22c62a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f77ddb2756340c1b05381674ca025d52998005e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d950e98f74af9611925a5226edced02155f6ed1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6df4f05bc2991467939d7d80b6f7e121559cc3df", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1e995498d29784a06a2b2899370a1926cfc8410d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/498386b6d402737db1e2eeed4c385acbf0ef9e34"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wq34-548c-54v3", "CVE-2026-80851"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16e33b3e-08cb-3d4b-82f6-fa4555e654d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "19f945bf-06bd-3333-afb4-29c2c41cf760", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2ee3215c-b565-39d2-a827-557af4c6d40b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "459aa660eb1d8ce67080da1983bb81d716aa5a69 <3d950e98f74af9611925a5226edced02155f6ed1"}, {"id": "41e5f24e-0cfc-3c0a-8ef0-59bd4cb90c32", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "47a7ceb9-d239-3092-984a-872b1bc7e085", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "459aa660eb1d8ce67080da1983bb81d716aa5a69 <1e995498d29784a06a2b2899370a1926cfc8410d"}, {"id": "66c1462f-6b20-3ab5-91ff-8b04267e456e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "8785f0f8-f302-313d-8bd1-753387ef74b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "95579953-4bcb-3c34-b208-6c22914d1b31", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "459aa660eb1d8ce67080da1983bb81d716aa5a69 <6df4f05bc2991467939d7d80b6f7e121559cc3df"}, {"id": "971d573f-653a-3186-8f4b-f66288506d4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "9e1cb7d8-8962-360a-9caa-8c612f9b5906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.7"}, {"id": "9e753497-3794-38d7-ad15-363cef95b0b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "459aa660eb1d8ce67080da1983bb81d716aa5a69 <5f77ddb2756340c1b05381674ca025d52998005e"}, {"id": "b142512a-b4ad-3c41-8575-9e247e7ef7c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "c09fd3ee-c3ae-326f-b7fe-82b3ac0e5825", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "459